<%# Shared visual spectator cluster for multiplayer game rooms (Durak,
    Sunduchki, Battleship, Pong, Connect Four) - a pile of little "viewer"
    icons standing in for the numeric "N watching" text those pages already
    show elsewhere. Wired by public/js/games/spectatorCluster.js's
    window.initSpectatorCluster() - a game view just includes this partial
    and its client calls that once, then feeds it a live spectator count.

    TWO markup variants, both rendered unconditionally and switched purely by
    a CSS breakpoint (never by embedWatch or anything else server-side):
      - #spectator-cluster: the original fixed panel in the page's unused
        left-hand margin, shown only at the xl breakpoint (`hidden xl:flex`)
        where that margin actually exists, hidden entirely at 0 viewers via
        inline style (see spectatorCluster.js) which wins the cascade either
        way, so JS can force it off even on a wide viewport.
      - #spectator-cluster-inline: the opposite breakpoint (`flex xl:hidden`),
        flowing in the normal page layout instead of floating - for whichever
        context has no such margin. Watching a specific room now ONLY happens
        through the cross-game spectator-hub embed (the per-room "Watch"
        button was removed in its favor) - that embed iframe is capped well
        under xl by the hub's own layout (views/gameWatch.ejs's 1fr/20rem
        grid), so the fixed variant above would never be visible there. But a
        spectator opening a `?watch=` link directly in a normal wide tab gets
        the exact same margin a player does - embedWatch is true in BOTH
        cases, so it can't tell them apart; only an actual CSS breakpoint can.
        Both games that use this (Durak/Sunduchki) include this partial once,
        right near their room header, so the inline variant sits near the top
        with no scrolling needed - the fixed variant doesn't care where in
        the DOM it lives, since it's viewport-positioned either way.

    initSpectatorCluster()/initSpectatorEmotePicker() each build whichever of
    the two variants exist on the page and update both from one call, so
    nothing here needs to know which is actually visible.

    The picker lets Durak/Sunduchki's own spectators change which pile icon
    represents THEM (realtime/spectatorEmotes.js's closed id set) instead of
    the plain default viewer image - wired by
    public/js/games/spectatorEmotePicker.js's window.initSpectatorEmotePicker().
    Opt-in via the `withEmotePicker: true` local (only those two games' own
    includes pass it) rather than rendered unconditionally: an <img> loads its
    src regardless of the "hidden" attribute on an ancestor, so leaving this
    markup in for Battleship/Pong/Connect Four would make every one of their
    pages eagerly fetch all 6 emote images (one of them ~650KB) for a picker
    those games never show. %>
<% const spectatorEmoteList = [
  ['default', '/images/games/spectator-viewer.png', 'spectatorEmoteDefault'],
  ['binoculous', '/images/games/spectator-emotes/binoculous.webp', 'spectatorEmoteBinoculous'],
  ['hmm', '/images/games/spectator-emotes/hmm.webp', 'spectatorEmoteHmm'],
  ['peepoblanket', '/images/games/spectator-emotes/peepoblanket.webp', 'spectatorEmotePeepoblanket'],
  ['peepoclap', '/images/games/spectator-emotes/peepoclap.webp', 'spectatorEmotePeepoclap'],
  ['peepocheer', '/images/games/spectator-emotes/peepocheer.webp', 'spectatorEmotePeepocheer'],
]; %>
<div id="spectator-cluster"
     class="hidden xl:flex fixed left-6 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 z-30 flex-col items-center gap-1.5 pointer-events-none">
  <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500"><%= t('games.spectatorsLabel') %></p>
  <div id="spectator-cluster-pile" class="relative w-40 h-40"></div>
  <% if (locals.withEmotePicker) { %>
  <div id="spectator-emote-picker" class="pointer-events-auto flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-1 w-32" hidden>
    <% spectatorEmoteList.forEach(function (e) { %>
      <button type="button" data-emote-id="<%= e[0] %>"
              class="w-6 h-6 rounded bg-neutral-800/80 hover:bg-neutral-700 p-0.5 transition-colors"
              title="<%= t('games.' + e[2]) %>">
        <img src="<%= e[1] %>" alt="<%= t('games.' + e[2]) %>" class="w-full h-full object-contain">
      </button>
    <% }); %>
  </div>
  <% } %>
</div>
<div id="spectator-cluster-inline" class="flex xl:hidden flex-col items-center gap-1.5 my-3">
  <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500"><%= t('games.spectatorsLabel') %></p>
  <div id="spectator-cluster-inline-pile" class="relative w-40 h-40"></div>
  <% if (locals.withEmotePicker) { %>
  <div id="spectator-emote-picker-inline" class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-1 w-32" hidden>
    <% spectatorEmoteList.forEach(function (e) { %>
      <button type="button" data-emote-id="<%= e[0] %>"
              class="w-6 h-6 rounded bg-neutral-800/80 hover:bg-neutral-700 p-0.5 transition-colors"
              title="<%= t('games.' + e[2]) %>">
        <img src="<%= e[1] %>" alt="<%= t('games.' + e[2]) %>" class="w-full h-full object-contain">
      </button>
    <% }); %>
  </div>
  <% } %>
</div>
